// Title: HackTool - SharpLDAPmonitor Execution
// Sigma ID: 9f8fc146-1d1a-4dbf-b8fd-dfae15e08541
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-12-30 | Modified: 2023-02-14
// ATT&CK: discovery
// Description: Detects execution of the SharpLDAPmonitor. Which can monitor the creation, deletion and changes
//   to LDAP objects.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/p0dalirius/LDAPmonitor
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_sharp_ldap_monitor.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\SharpLDAPmonitor.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "SharpLDAPmonitor.exe") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "/user:" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/pass:" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/dcip:")
